# TypeScript Rules

## Type Safety
- Always use explicit types for function parameters and return values
- Avoid `any` type - use `unknown` or specific types instead
- Use type guards for runtime type checking
- Prefer interfaces over types for object shapes

## Environment Variables
- Never use non-null assertions (`!`) on environment variables
- Always validate environment variables with proper error messages
- Use type-safe environment variable access

```typescript
// ❌ Bad
const apiUrl = process.env.API_URL!

// ✅ Good
const apiUrl = process.env.API_URL
if (!apiUrl) {
  throw new Error('API_URL environment variable is required')
}
```

## Error Handling
- Use proper error types and custom error classes
- Always handle async operations with try-catch
- Provide meaningful error messages

## React/Next.js Specific
- Use proper typing for props and state
- Prefer `React.FC` or explicit prop types
- Use Next.js specific types like `NextPage`, `GetServerSideProps`